course: dictionary
lesson: 3755
title: Feeling flustered
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Flustered describes someone who feels nervous, confused and a bit embarrassed, usually because they are rushed or things are going wrong. Picture someone who is late, drops their books and goes red in the face. That is flustered.
explain: Look at the words around it. «A busy or flustered teacher who says "sit down" isn't your enemy: pick a better moment.» Busy and rushed suggest the teacher is in a muddle, not angry or cruel. The clues show what the word means.
explain: Flustered can also be a verb. To fluster someone is to make them feel this way. A sudden question might fluster you. Try the swap test: put "in a muddle" in place of flustered and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Flustered means nervous, confused and a bit embarrassed.
fact: Flustered often means you are rushed or things are going wrong.
fact: To fluster someone is to make them feel flustered.
fact: Useful phrases are get flustered, look flustered and all flustered.
fact: Old words: «I fancy» means I think, «made believe» means pretended, and «a deal too flustered» means much too upset and muddled.
exercise: «A busy or flustered teacher who says "sit down" isn't your enemy.» What does flustered mean here? | Calm and relaxed | *Nervous, rushed and a bit muddled | Angry and cruel | Fast asleep
exercise: Ella drops her books, goes red and mixes up her times. How is she feeling? | Bored | Proud | *Flustered | Sleepy
exercise: What does "to fluster someone" mean? | To ask someone a question | To calm someone right down | *To make someone feel nervous and muddled | To hide something from them
test: Jamal looks flustered when he cannot find his PE kit. Which word means the same as flustered? | Hungry | Cheerful | Confident | *Muddled
test: «Don't fluster me while I'm counting.» What is the speaker asking for? | To sit down quietly | To be given a prize | *Not to rush them or confuse them | To count faster
exam: Read this: «Mrs Patel got flustered when the projector stopped working.» What does flustered tell you about Mrs Patel? | She was bored and tired | *She felt rushed, nervous and a bit muddled | She was delighted by the new screen | She was angry and wanted to shout
